# Wave W17-M (Route 105): tomb sand — tomb-shore sand, stone-pale and quiet, the shore of a drowned ruin with a few grey stone chips ground into it (design: island ruins keep their counsel under the swell). Route 105’s own shore — the palest, greyest sand in the surf arc, split from Route 106’s bright town sand by value.
